    "problem_statement": "# `--scalar` option removed from CLI\n\n### Bug description\n\nThe `--scalar` option has been removed from the glom CLI, which breaks my scripts that rely on this functionality. When using the CLI to extract a single value, I need the output without quotes or whitespace for easier usage in shell scripts.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create a simple JSON file with a scalar value:\n```json\n{\"value\": 42}\n```\n\n2. Try to extract the scalar value using the `--scalar` option:\n```shell\nglom data.json value --scalar\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe command should output just `42` without quotes or newlines, making it easy to use in shell scripts.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe command fails with an error about an unknown option `--scalar`, or if using an older version of the code that had this option, it outputs `42` with quotes and a newline like this:\n```\n\"42\"\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nThis breaks shell scripts that pipe glom output directly into other commands, where the extra quotes and whitespace cause issues.\n\n### Reproduction script\n\n```shell\necho '{\"value\": 42}' > test.json\nglom test.json value --scalar\n# Should output: 42\n# Instead fails or outputs: \"42\"\n```\n\n### Version information\n\nglom version: latest from master branch\n\n### OS / Environment\n\nLinux (but should affect all platforms)"
  }
}
